WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.339
Inspecting an open design is only part of assessing confidence.

2
00:00:06.339 --> 00:00:13.584
Tests check particular behaviors, a reference model supports comparison,

3
00:00:13.584 --> 00:00:21.634
a coverage plan defines goals, and regressions check for problems after changes.

4
00:00:21.634 --> 00:00:24.552
These activities reduce risk.

5
00:00:24.552 --> 00:00:29.583
Reference-model agreement is not exhaustive proof,

6
00:00:29.583 --> 00:00:35.520
and regression does not guarantee that defects never recur.

7
00:00:35.520 --> 00:00:40.652
Interpret coverage with its plan, target and tools;

8
00:00:40.652 --> 00:00:47.494
the pinned verif documentation scopes its coverage-plan flow to VCS.

9
00:00:47.494 --> 00:00:55.041
The named example is cv32a60x-v6.0.0, released on April twenty-third, 2025.

10
00:00:55.041 --> 00:01:02.185
The publisher states TRL5 for a specific configuration: OBI, no caches,

11
00:01:02.185 --> 00:01:06.110
zero PMP entries and disabled Zifencei.

12
00:01:06.110 --> 00:01:14.361
The release resolves to b1f80bd, while our general verification reading comes from

13
00:01:14.361 --> 00:01:15.166
81245a4.

14
00:01:15.166 --> 00:01:22.008
The review questions are not the complete historical release report.

15
00:01:22.008 --> 00:01:29.756
TRL5 neither transfers automatically to the family nor represents independent

16
00:01:29.756 --> 00:01:32.674
certification by this course.

17
00:01:32.674 --> 00:01:38.309
Zero PMP entries does not exclude all system protection.

18
00:01:38.309 --> 00:01:45.252
A changed cache or interface requires reassessing goals and evidence.

19
00:01:45.252 --> 00:01:53.302
Likewise, a merged implementation does not establish which options were enabled,

20
00:01:53.302 --> 00:01:56.623
tests covered, or systems booted.

21
00:01:56.623 --> 00:02:02.660
Preserve configuration, version and evidence scope together.

